{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfSdM37yAvQHPEiahaTvJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Summary of Repository Findings:**\n\n- **Order.kt:11-16** - Order data class lacks status field\n- **OrderController.kt:17-46** - Has create, getById, list; needs cancel endpoint\n- **OrderRepository.kt:10-27** - Standard in-memory CRUD, sufficient for the feature\n- **Shipment.kt:9-27** - Has ShipmentStatus enum (CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED) already\n- **ShipmentController.kt:26-44** - Create checks duplicate; needs validation for cancelled orders\n- **ShipmentRepository.kt:10-27** - Lacks findByOrderId method; need to add it\n- **ApiException.kt:11-30** - ConflictException and ResourceNotFoundException patterns are established\n- **ApiError.kt:31-37** - ErrorCode enum; needs codes for order/shipment conflicts\n\n**Conventions observed:**\n- Controllers throw ApiExceptions; GlobalExceptionHandler converts them to error envelope\n- Tests use MockMvc with jsonPath assertions checking both status and error body shape\n- BeforeEach resets repositories\n- Each endpoint has dedicated test class\n\n**Affected files (unavoidable changes):**\n1. Order.kt - must add status field\n2. OrderController.kt - must add cancel endpoint\n3. ShipmentRepository.kt - must add findByOrderId() method\n4. ShipmentController.kt - must validate cancelled orders before creating shipments\n5. ApiError.kt - must add error codes\n6. OrderControllerTest.kt - must test cancel scenarios\n\n**Risks:**\n- Order serialization might change JSON shape\n- Order cancellation is not atomic in the current in-memory model\n- Tests must remain passing\n\n**Open questions:** None identified that change the requirement's meaning.\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed change:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** - Add an OrderStatus enum (ACTIVE, CANCELLED) and add a `status: OrderStatus` field to the Order data class, defaulting new orders to ACTIVE.\n\n2. **ApiError.kt** - Add two error codes: `SHIPMENT_CONFIRMED` (when canceling order with confirmed shipment) and `ORDER_CANCELLED` (when creating shipment for cancelled order).\n\n3. **OrderRepository.kt** - No changes needed; existing methods suffice.\n\n4. **ShipmentRepository.kt** - Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` to find all shipments for an order.\n\n5. **OrderController.kt** - Add `@PostMapping(\"/{orderId}/cancel\")` endpoint that:\n   - Returns 404 if order doesn't exist\n   - If order is CANCELLED, succeeds with 200 and returns the order (idempotent)\n   - If any shipment is CONFIRMED, throws ConflictException with SHIPMENT_CONFIRMED and changes nothing\n   - Otherwise, transitions order to CANCELLED, updates all CREATED shipments to CANCELLED, returns updated order with 200\n\n6. **ShipmentController.kt** - In the create endpoint, add validation after line 33 to check if the order exists and is CANCELLED; if so, throw ConflictException with ORDER_CANCELLED.\n\n7. **OrderControllerTest.kt** - Add 5 test cases:\n   - Cancel an active order succeeds and returns CANCELLED status\n   - Cancel returns updated CREATED shipments to CANCELLED\n   - Cancel an already-cancelled order succeeds (idempotent)\n   - Cancel fails 409 if order has a CONFIRMED shipment, no state changes\n   - Cancel returns 404 for unknown order\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n- Adding OrderStatus as a field in CreateOrderRequest: Rejected because the ticket specifies new orders should be ACTIVE, not customer-specified.\n- Implementing cancel as a PATCH instead of POST: Rejected because the ticket explicitly asks for POST.\n- Using a separate cancellation service: Rejected because the inline logic in the controller follows existing patterns.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n1. **Cancel active order with only CREATED shipments:**\n   - Read order from repository\n   - Validate it exists → 404 if not (ResourceNotFoundException)\n   - If status is CANCELLED → return 200 with order (idempotent)\n   - Find all shipments by orderId\n   - Check if any shipment is CONFIRMED → 409 ConflictException if found\n   - Update order status to CANCELLED and save\n   - Update all CREATED shipments to CANCELLED and save each\n   - Return 200 with updated order\n\n2. **Attempted cancel with CONFIRMED shipment:**\n   - Read order\n   - Find shipments\n   - Detect CONFIRMED status\n   - Throw ConflictException (SHIPMENT_CONFIRMED, 409)\n   - No changes persisted\n\n3. **Create shipment for cancelled order:**\n   - Read order from repository\n   - Check status is not CANCELLED\n   - If CANCELLED, throw ConflictException (ORDER_CANCELLED, 409)\n   - Otherwise proceed normally\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n- **Test 1:** Cancel active order → verifies order status changes to CANCELLED, endpoint returns 200\n- **Test 2:** Cancel active order with CREATED shipment → verifies shipment status also becomes CANCELLED\n- **Test 3:** Cancel already-cancelled order → verifies it returns 200 and doesn't change anything (idempotent)\n- **Test 4:** Cancel with CONFIRMED shipment → verifies 409 returned, order stays ACTIVE, shipment stays CONFIRMED\n- **Test 5:** Cancel unknown order → verifies 404 with ORDER_NOT_FOUND code\n- **Test 6:** Create shipment for cancelled order → verifies 409 with ORDER_CANCELLED code\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1727,"cache_read_input_tokens":21070,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1727},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2c35a428-e635-4532-b6e1-d3ac1f9a700d","uuid":"5dc62c46-bbbf-4cc8-8e90-17d5f4ba0c1e","timestamp":"2026-09-26T19:47:15.280Z","request_id":"req_011CfSdM2mNsyNK