cancelling an unknown order returns 404\" - verify 404 for unknown order\n   - Test: \"rejects shipment creation for a cancelled order with 409\" - verify shipment blocking\n\n6. **No new Maven dependency appears** ✅\n   - No changes to pom.xml\n\n7. **No unrelated production file changes** ✅\n   - Only changed: Order.kt, OrderController.kt, ShipmentController.kt, ShipmentRepository.kt, ApiError.kt\n   - Only changed tests: OrderControllerTest.kt, ShipmentControllerTest.kt\n   - All changes are required for the feature\n\n**Diff review:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** - Added OrderStatus enum and status field with ACTIVE default. Required because order needs to track cancellation state. ✅\n\n2. **ApiError.kt** - Added ORDER_CANCELLED and SHIPMENT_CONFIRMED error codes. Required for the new error cases. ✅\n\n3. **OrderController.kt** - Added cancel endpoint and injected ShipmentRepository. Required to implement the cancel feature. ✅\n\n4. **ShipmentRepository.kt** - Added findByOrderId method. Required to find shipments for cancellation. ✅\n\n5. **ShipmentController.kt** - Added validation to block shipment creation for cancelled orders. Required by spec. ✅\n\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt** - Added 5 new tests covering cancel scenarios. Required for test coverage. ✅\n\n7. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** - Added 1 new test for cancelled order shipment rejection. Required for test coverage. ✅\n\n**Unresolved findings:** None. All acceptance criteria are implemented and tested.\n\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n\n```\nRequirement   Add POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint that cancels active orders, transitions order to CANCELLED status, cancels CREATED shipments, prevents shipment creation for cancelled orders, and handles all error cases idempotently.\n\nChanged       Order.kt: Added OrderStatus enum and status field to track order cancellation state\n              OrderController.kt: Added cancel endpoint with all validation and state transition logic\n              ShipmentRepository.kt: Added findByOrderId method to query shipments by order ID\n              ShipmentController.kt: Added validation to prevent shipment creation for cancelled orders\n              ApiError.kt: Added ORDER_CANCELLED and SHIPMENT_CONFIRMED error codes\n              OrderControllerTest.kt: Added 5 tests for cancel endpoint scenarios (active cancel, shipment cancellation, idempotency, CONFIRMED blocking, not found)\n              ShipmentControllerTest.kt: Added 1 test for shipment creation rejection on cancelled order\n\nTests         Test 1 - cancels an active order and returns CANCELLED status: Verifies order status changes to CANCELLED\n              Test 2 - cancelling an order cancels its CREATED shipments: Verifies CREATED shipments are transitioned to CANCELLED\n              Test 3 - cancelling an already-cancelled order succeeds (idempotent): Verifies idempotency returns 200\n              Test 4 - cancelling an order with CONFIRMED shipment fails with 409: Verifies atomicity (all-or-nothing) with proper error code\n              Test 5 - cancelling an unknown order returns 404: Verifies 404 with ORDER_NOT_FOUND code\n              Test 6 - rejects shipment creation for a cancelled order with 409: Verifies shipment creation is blocked with ORDER_CANCELLED code\n\nVerification  Command: ./mvnw test from sample-service/ directory\n              Result: 19 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors\n              BUILD SUCCESS\n\nNot done      Nothing - all acceptance criteria implemented and verified\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3309,"cache_read_input_tokens":35351,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3309},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2c35a428-e635-4532-b6e1-d3ac1f9a700d